@attribute [Route("/components/" + nameof(HxInputDateRange))]

<ApiDoc Type="typeof(HxInputDateRange<TValue>)">
    <DocAlert Type="DocAlertType.Warning">
        <code>HxInputDateRange</code> does not support additional <code>InputGroups</code>. Learn more about them <a href="/components/Inputs#InputGroups">here</a>.
    </DocAlert>

    <DocHeading Title="Basic usage" />
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxInputDateRange_Demo)" Tabs="false" />

	<DocHeading Title="DateOnly ranges" />
	<p>
		Bind directly to a <code>Havit.DateOnlyRange</code> property (from Havit.Core 2.0.41 or later).
		The component infers its <code>TValue</code> from the binding and preserves the original model field for validation.
		Both endpoints are nullable; the default value is an empty range. Open ranges are supported.
	</p>
	<Demo Type="typeof(HxInputDateRange_Demo_DateOnly)" />
	<p>
		Use <code>InputDateRangePredefinedRangesItem&lt;DateOnlyRange&gt;</code> and
		<code>InputDateRangeSettings&lt;DateOnlyRange&gt;</code> for date-only presets and settings.
		Date-only defaults are configured with <code>HxInputDateRange.DateOnlyDefaults</code>;
		<code>HxInputDateRange.Defaults</code> continues to configure DateTime ranges independently.
	</p>
	<p>
		For compatibility with <code>HxInputDate</code> and <code>HxCalendar</code>, <code>MinDate</code>,
		<code>MaxDate</code>, <code>FromCalendarDisplayMonth</code>, <code>ToCalendarDisplayMonth</code>,
		and calendar customization callbacks still use <code>DateTime</code>, including in settings.
		The internal conversion of date-only values uses midnight without UTC or time-zone conversion.
		<code>TimeProvider</code> controls the calendar's current date, not the selected dates' time zone.
	</p>
	<DocHeading Title="Migration to the generic component" />
	<p>
		Existing Razor bindings to <code>DateTimeRange</code> keep the same markup.
		Explicit C# component references (including <code>@@ref</code> fields), component subclasses and render-tree calls
		now use <code>HxInputDateRange&lt;DateTimeRange&gt;</code>.
		Specify <code>TValue</code> explicitly when there is no binding from which to infer it.
		The non-generic settings and predefined-item classes remain available for DateTime ranges;
		their range collections now expose the generic item type.
	</p>
	<p>
		Remove application-side DateTime conversion properties when adopting <code>DateOnlyRange</code>.
		A thin wrapper can forward <code>Value</code>, <code>ValueChanged</code> and <code>ValueExpression</code>
		directly, along with presentation and validation parameters. No separate validation message is needed.
	</p>

    <DocHeading Title="Calendar icon" />
    <p>
        An optional icon can be added using the <code>CalendarIcon</code> parameter.<br />
        You can set the icon for all instances of <code>HxInputDateRange</code> by setting the <code>HxInputDateRange.Defaults.CalendarIcon</code> static property.
    </p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxInputDateRange_Demo_CalendarIcon)" />

    <DocHeading Title="Hide Clear button in calendars" Id="clear-button" />
    <p>The <i>Clear</i> button in dropdown calendars can be hidden by setting <code>ShowClearButton="false"</code>.</p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxInputDateRange_Demo_ClearButton)" />

    <DocHeading Title="Predefined date ranges" />
    <p>You can add predefined date ranges with the <code>PredefinedDateRanges</code> parameter.</p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxInputDateRange_Demo_CustomRanges)" />
    <p>If you set <code>HxInputDateRange.Defaults.PredefinedDateRanges</code> as default ranges for the whole application, you can hide them on individual instances with <code>ShowPredefinedDateRanges="false"</code>.</p>

    <DocHeading Title="Dropdown calendars customization" />
    <p>
        You can change the rendering of weekend days by defining your own CSS rule for the <code>.weekend</code> class.
        The disabled days get the <code>.disabled</code> class.
    </p>
    <DocAlert Type="DocAlertType.Warning">
        Disabling dates with the techniques below won't prevent the user from entering disabled dates manually. You still have to validate the value.
    </DocAlert>

    <DocHeading Title="MinDate, MaxDate" Level="3" />
    <p>You can limit the enabled dates of the dropdown calendars (both <i>From</i> and <i>To</i> together) by setting <code>MinDate</code> and/or <code>MaxDate</code>.</p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxInputDateRange_Demo_MinDateMaxDate)" />

    <DocHeading Title="Calendar date customization" Level="3" />
    <p>
        You can customize the dates of the dropdown calendars with the <code>CalendarDateCustomizationProvider</code>. You can disable individual dates
        (<code>Enabled="false"</code>) or set a specific CSS class (<code>CssClass="...")</code>.
    </p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxInputDateRange_Demo_CalendarDateCustomization)" />

    <DocHeading Title="Calendar time zone" Level="3" />
    <p>
        You can customize the time zone of the dropdown calendar by supplying a custom <code>TimeProvider</code>.  See <a href="/components/HxCalendar#time-zones">HxCalendar time zones</a> for more details.
    </p>
</ApiDoc>